      "text": "Janauari Ecological Park and the Meeting of the Waters"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "287f09958cd3c4a1811f855be644cd007b675b52a889c5605191178af7e71dc5",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6ksoy5-ph2ue2h6fz",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "The morning begins with birdwatching and a visit to Janauari Ecological Park. Here you can see the flooded forest and the large leaves of the giant Amazon water lily, a species characteristic of the region’s waterways.\n\nExplore by canoe and along wooden boardwalks. Depending on the season and water level, you can look for wildlife in the treetops and by the water.\n\nDuring breakfast, the ship heads towards the Meeting of the Waters. Here, the dark waters of the Rio Negro run alongside the lighter waters of the Amazon, remaining distinct for a long stretch because of differences in temperature, density and current speed.\n\nAfter the Meeting of the Waters, the ship returns to Manaus. Along the way, you can see the port, floating docks, the market, the old customs house and the dome of the Amazon Theatre.\n\nThe cruise ends in Manaus."
    },
